    tools/make-aquarium iocean-tank-1 --into ~/coral-city/places/iocean-tank-1

Not a towing tank (that is tools/make-tank, whose whole point is that nothing
in it is chosen) and not a reef. This is the bench a person actually has: a
one-metre cube of glass on a steel stand, sand and rock and a few corals in
it, a handful of small fish, and around it the room — the desk with the
computer that flies the vehicle, the switch the tether runs to, a camera on a
gantry looking down, a fan that can blow across the surface, a pump that
makes a current, and the light over it all.

Everything here is **chosen**, and the record says so. The tank's size is the
one the user named; the rest is a plausible room, built so the vehicle can be
seen from outside the glass as well as through its own camera.

Metres, Z up, z = 0 at the still water surface, origin in the middle of the
tank, x towards the room's open side, y along the desk.
"""

